id: ops-gitr
title: Fix release publish-before-protected-main-push ordering
description: "The daily release workflow published to npm before pushing the version bump to protected main. The push was rejected with GH006 and set -e killed the job before the tag push, leaving npm ahead of git. Port the pm-beads fix: merge release metadata through a protected PR before publishing, then push only the tag."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-10T15:02:19.464Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-10T15:20:38.517Z"
author: pi-agent
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-10T15:02:37.405Z",pi-agent,"Ported the pm-beads release.yml transformation: added pull-requests:write permission, base_sha decide output, Check release ref step, Merge release metadata through protected PR step with merge-loop, Verify merged release step, and replaced Publish+Push-tag-and-main with Publish+Push-tag-only. dist/ is tracked in pm-ops so it is included in the verify diff list. The old Publish npm package and Push release tag and main steps were replaced with the four-step protected-PR flow."
  "2026-08-10T15:20:38.517Z",claude,"Greptile reviewed this change and reported that creating the release pull request with GITHUB_TOKEN suppresses its pull_request event so CI never starts. Measured against pm-changelog, the event is not suppressed: a CI run was created at 04:54:24Z with event pull_request for branch release/2026.8.9. The real blocker is that attempt 1 concluded action_required, meaning GitHub parked the run awaiting workflow approval because the fork pull request contributor approval policy is first_time_contributors and github-actions had no merged pull request in that repository yet. A parked run never appears in the status check rollup, so it is indistinguishable from a required check that failed. The merge wait now detects parked runs, reports the run URL, attempts approval using the actions write permission, and separates awaiting approval from a failed check in the deadline error."
body: ""
